<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mamai</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1380">1380</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mamai was an emir and military commander of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-horde">Golden Horde</a> who, during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-troubles">Great Troubles</a> after 1359, ruled its western half through a series of puppet khans. Not being a descendant of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genghis-khan">Genghis Khan</a>, he could not take the throne himself. His army was defeated by Grand Prince Dmitry of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-kulikovo">Battle of Kulikovo</a> in 1380, and he was killed soon after, having lost to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokhtamysh">Tokhtamysh</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mamai.jpg" alt="Mamai" width="159" height="181" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tibicena · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mamai.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
